NAME
    modules - DianaSh command modules and the settings service

SYNOPSIS
    man modules

DESCRIPTION
    A command module is a library of commands linked into or loaded by
    DianaSh. Its JSON manifest declares its module id, version, commands,
    aliases, claimed job prefixes (for ps(1) and kill(1)), requested
    services, permitted setting keys, and whether it may manage core
    approvals. The shell provides each module only the services offered
    by the host.

THE SETTINGS SERVICE
    The emusen.settings service (version 1) exposes console and per-game
    runtime settings, as well as core approval and revocation. Hosts
    that embed an EmuSen runtime provide this service; the standalone
    dianash(1) executable does not, and commands requiring it report
    that it is unavailable.

    Modules never access runtime settings directly. Each module manifest
    declares the exact setting keys it may read or write ("settings",
    such as Engine for cores(1)) and whether it may approve or revoke
    cores ("approvals"). The shell wraps the service in a per-module
    guard that permits only those declared keys; a module declaring none
    receives no settings service.

    Core approval is interactive-only: approval commands are accepted
    only when typed directly at the prompt, and are refused inside
    source(1) scripts, command substitutions $(...), or pipelines (the
    same restriction as trust(1)). Revoking an approval is permitted
    anywhere.

EXAMPLES
    cores default "PlayStation 2" Sapphire
    cores default --game /Games/ps2/jak.chd -
    cores approve pcee2

SEE ALSO
    cores(1), trust(1), dianash(1), hier(7)
